From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Build Firestore's dependencies from their vendored sources

A host's abseil got into the build through re2.  Firestore does
find_package(re2 QUIET), and a distribution's re2Config.cmake does
find_dependency(absl).  Once absl:: targets exist, gRPC, protobuf and
utf8_range use them instead of building their own.  On Fedora with
abseil-cpp-devel and re2-devel installed, the result needs about a hundred
of that host's libabsl_*.so at runtime, test helpers included, at whatever
version the distribution ships.  On a host without them the same sources
build abseil 20240722 statically.

Don't look for re2: gRPC builds its own either way, since Firestore tests
RE2_FOUND and re2's config sets re2_FOUND.  Disable find_package(absl) for
the whole build, so anything else that reaches for an installed abseil
fails at configure instead of linking it.  And turn off gRPC's libsystemd,
which it links when the host has it, for server socket activation a client
never uses.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9b59b6a..f43b67e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -273,6 +273,22 @@ set(FIRESTORE_INCLUDE_OBJC OFF CACHE BOOL "Disabled for the CPP SDK")
 # Disable re2 build tests
 set(RE2_BUILD_TESTING OFF CACHE BOOL "")
 
+# Firestore's dependencies build from the sources they vendor, whatever the
+# host has installed. A host's abseil got in through re2: Firestore's
+# find_package(re2 QUIET) loads a distribution's re2Config.cmake, which does
+# find_dependency(absl), and once absl:: targets exist gRPC, protobuf and
+# utf8_range use them instead of building their own. The library then needs
+# that host's libabsl_*.so at runtime, at whatever version it ships.
+#
+# re2 is not looked for: gRPC builds its own either way, since Firestore tests
+# RE2_FOUND and re2's config sets re2_FOUND. abseil is not either, so anything
+# else that reaches for an installed one fails here rather than linking it.
+set(CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_re2 ON CACHE BOOL "Build the vendored re2")
+set(CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_absl ON CACHE BOOL "Build the vendored abseil")
+# gRPC links libsystemd when the host has it, for server socket activation,
+# which a client never uses.
+set(gRPC_USE_SYSTEMD OFF CACHE STRING "No socket activation")
+
 if(FIREBASE_CPP_USE_PRIOR_GRADLE_BUILD)
   # Gradle now adds a random hash to each separate NDK cmake build.
   # Scan the previously built directories to find the one containing app's header.
